Hearing grandsire word Fire rises holding Vaidehi on lap --- Fire presents sunlike gold-ornamented red-clad black-curly-haired girl with unfaded garlands --- Fire witness says Vaidehi has no sin by word mind thought or eye well-conducted never transgressed --- Fire says lustful Ravana bore helpless parted Sita from lonely forest and confined her guarded with mind on Rama --- Fire says rakshasi-guarded threatened tempted Mithili never thought of demon with soul fixed on Rama --- Fire bids Raghava take pure sinless commanding no blame --- Mighty Rama tells gods Sita needed purification before three worlds after long Ravana house stay lest saints call Rama lustful childish --- Rama says he knows sole-hearted devoted Mithili guarding his mind --- Rama says for conviction of three worlds he overlooked Vaidehi entering fire guarded by own splendour as ocean by shore --- Rama says evil one could not assault blazing Mithili even in mind inseparable as sunlight from sun pure in three worlds like fame --- Rama vows to honour loving honoured friendly words and praised for deed reunites with beloved and enjoys happiness